     \/\/ [\"\/usr\/lib\", \"\/usr\/local\/bin\"]","paths.longestPrefix(of: \"\/usr\/bin\/swift\").map { String($0) } \/\/ \"\/usr\/bin\""]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Iteration visits each key before the keys it is a prefix of. When the symbols are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"Comparable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", each vertex keeps its children sorted, so the keys come in lexicographic order;","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"otherwise children come in the order they were first added.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The vertices live in flat arrays with ","type":"text"},{"code":"Int32","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" links, and the edge labels are slices of one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"buffer of symbols, so the tree holds fewer than 2³¹ − 1 vertices and label symbols, and copying","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it copies a few arrays only when one copy is mutated.","type":"text"}]}]}],"references":{"doc://Tries/documentation/Tries/RadixTree/Encodable-Implementations":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/RadixTree\/Encodable-Implementations","role":"collectionGroup","title":"Encodable Implementations","abstract":[],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/tries\/radixtree\/encodable-implementations","kind":"article"},"doc://Tries/documentation/Tries/Trie":{"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A set of sequences kept in a trie: a tree whose edges carry symbols and whose root-to-vertex"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"paths spell the keys (Fredkin, 1960)."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/Trie","url":"\/documentation\/tries\/trie","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Trie"}],"type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Trie"}],"title":"Trie"},"doc://Tries/documentat